Brand cyber overlay style guide
title end

paragraph start
Cyber overlays are thin graphic layers over monochrome footage, such as scan lines, grid lines, data readouts, glitch frames and corner brackets. They are made in white first, and red or purple only where the palette rules allow.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Each overlay needs a reason, such as marking a title, a change of section or an emphasis. If it only decorates, remove it. Overlays never cover the face, the subject or caption text.
paragraph end

code start
language: text
overlay name, purpose, colour, where it may appear, where it must not appear
code end

